<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21332] lnet: ping dump restarts and leaks when an entry does not fit</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21332</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;lnet_ping_show_dump() handles a failed genlmsg_put() in the loop over&lt;br/&gt;
failed pings by jumping to send_error with -EMSGSIZE.  It does not save&lt;br/&gt;
plist-&amp;gt;lgpl_index, does not free the lgpl_list genradix of that round,&lt;br/&gt;
and passes the NULL hdr to genlmsg_cancel().&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On a 6.7+ kernel netlink_dump() retries a dump that returns -EMSGSIZE&lt;br/&gt;
with data already in the skb.  The retry starts from the stale index,&lt;br/&gt;
so every peer is pinged again, the genradix of the previous round&lt;br/&gt;
leaks, and the next round can use the freed list.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: save lgpl_index and free the round's list on the error path, and&lt;br/&gt;
trim the skb so an entry that does not fit by itself returns with an&lt;br/&gt;
empty skb.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
